.TH MSEPARATE 1 "November 2026" "mseparate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mseparate \- analyze audio and prepare a multi-model separation plan
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mseparate
.I input
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mseparate
is an independent command for technical audio analysis and preparation of a future multi-model source-separation plan. This foundation release performs signal measurements only. It does not run neural inference and does not modify the input audio.
.PP
The existing
.B melband-roformer
and
.B separate
workflows are unchanged.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --analysis-only
Analyze the input without displaying an execution plan.
.TP
.B --plan-only
Analyze the input and display the currently available execution plan.
.TP
.B --output-dir DIR
Directory used for a requested report file.
.TP
.B --report [PATH]
Write a JSON report. If PATH is omitted, use mseparate-report.json in the output directory.
.TP
.B --models-dir DIR
Override the local model storage directory.
.TP
.B --device auto|cuda|cpu
Record the intended compute device. Neural inference is not enabled in this release.
.TP
.B --prepare-models
Verify or download assets for registry models whose license and required checksums have been reviewed.
.TP
.B --no-download
Verify local assets only; never access the network. Applies to --prepare-models.
.TP
.B --download-timeout SECONDS
Per-request network timeout (default 30 seconds).
.TP
.B --download-retries N
Maximum attempts per asset (default 3).
.TP
.B --max-depth N
Set the maximum refinement depth for the execution plan.
.TP
.B --verbose
Print additional diagnostics.
.TP
.B --version
Print the mseparate version.
.SH DATA
By default, persistent data is stored under
.I ~/.local/share/mseparate/
with separate models, registry, cache and jobs directories. The
.B MSEPARATE_HOME
environment variable overrides the root directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Analysis completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Report could not be written.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments or input/registry error.
.SH NOTES
The initial registry is empty by design. A model must have reviewed license metadata, verified assets and a compatible backend before it can be scheduled. No model quality or separation result is implied by this analysis-only foundation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR melband-roformer (1)
